From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: the session's Linux programs' windows in Task View

David: a Linux terminal was not shown in Task View (the desktop overview).
Its window is a top-level beside Wine's desktop; the taskbar knew it (0496,
by a hidden stand-in window per Linux window) but Task View listed only
Wine's windows. Task View now shows each as a card with its icon and title,
on every desktop; a click brings it forward (sg-lockctl XACTIVATE), its menu
closes it (XCLOSE), and it is not dragged to another desktop.

Gate: make test-taskview-linux.
